 R←Test_Open_087(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;tempDir;parms;success;log;qdmx;threw;list
⍝ A project that fails to open half-way must still be recognised as an open one, and must therefore
⍝ be closable.\\
⍝ The Link is created early in `OpenProject` and the configuration used to be injected at the very
⍝ end. `ListOpenProjects` keeps only namespaces carrying a `CiderConfig`, so anything that threw in
⍝ between became invisible to it - and `]Cider.CloseProject` works from that list, while
⍝ `CheckForAlreadyOpened` asks Link alone and so refused to open the project again. The only way out
⍝ was `⎕SE.Link.Break` by hand or `)CLEAR`.\\
⍝ Batch mode makes this deterministic: the `Assert~parms.batch` calls throw by design there.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '∘∘∘ ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 tempDir←∆GetFolderInTempDir⊃⎕SI
 #.⎕SHADOW'TEMP' ⋄ 'TEMP'#.⎕NS''
 tempDir ⎕NCOPY⍠('Wildcard' 1)⊣##.CiderConfig.HOME,'/TestData/InvalidVersionNumber/*'
⍝ The sub-directory stops `CheckForTatinPackages` from re-installing, which would need a Registry.
⍝ The invalid entry then makes `LoadTatinDependencies` fail, and in batch mode it fails without
⍝ asking anybody, so no Registry is involved at any point.
 3 ⎕MKDIR tempDir,'/packages/dummy-pkg-1.0.0'
 (⊂'this is not a package id')⎕NPUT(tempDir,'/packages/apl-dependencies.txt')1

 parms←##.Cider.CreateOpenParms ⍬
 parms.folder←tempDir
 parms.parent←'#.TEMP'
 parms.batch←1
 parms.ignoreUserExec←1

 threw←0
 :Trap 0
     (success log)←##.Cider.OpenProject parms
 :Else
     threw←1
     qdmx←⎕DMX
 :EndTrap
 →T.GoToTidyUp~threw                                    ⍝ In batch mode this must throw ...
 →T.GoToTidyUp~∨/'needs attention'⍷qdmx.EM              ⍝ ... and for the expected reason

⍝ The Link is there, so the project must be recognisable as open, which takes a `CiderConfig`
 →T.GoToTidyUp 9≠#.TEMP.UpdatePkgs.⎕NC'CiderConfig'
 →T.GoToTidyUp~(⊂'#.TEMP.UpdatePkgs')∊(##.Cider.ListOpenProjects 0)[;1]

⍝ ... and closing it must work, which is the point of all of the above
 →T.GoToTidyUp 1≠0 ##.Cider.CloseProject'#.TEMP.UpdatePkgs'
 →T.GoToTidyUp(⊂'#.TEMP.UpdatePkgs')∊(##.Cider.ListOpenProjects 0)[;1]

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 {}⎕SE.Link.Break'#.TEMP.UpdatePkgs'                    ⍝ No check: when all is well it is not linked anymore
 {}FilesAndDirs.RmDirByForce tempDir,'/..'
⍝Done
